  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "## Recommendation: HOLD\n\n**Summary:** This layer adds conservative read-only Z24S8 alias admission and checked scratch-buffer sizing. It is rebased onto refreshed #287; four maintained groups pass, including 19 added independent negative cases. Source review found no blocker; the helpers have no production caller in this layer.\n**Remaining:** Parent #287 merge and current-head CI. Runtime ownership/conversion qualification belongs to #289/#290.\n\n### Problem\n\nSharing a guest address does not prove that a linear depth producer can safely feed a swizzled view. Format, layout, DMA identity, extents and current producer state must qualify before recording conversion.\n\n### What this PR changes\n\n`surface-alias-map.c/.h` checks linear producer/read-only swizzled destination, guest Z24S8 and matching supported host format, scale1/no AA, matching address/DMA/pitch, initialized non-superseded producer without pending transfers, sufficient extents and the bounded producer size. A separate checked planner sizes aligned depth/stencil scratch regions. The header explicitly leaves newest-producer ownership and profitability to the runtime caller.\n\nTests compare guest Morton layout, reject invalid shapes, check admission and verify buffer sizing. Added cases independently mutate color/layout/initialization/download state, guest/host formats, DMA length, pitch, short extent, oversized/empty dimensions and null pointers. No product algorithm was expanded.\n\n### Why this approach\n\nPure bounded admission keeps unsupported cases on the existing path. It performs integer checks and a short Morton validation loop; no allocation, surface traversal, byte comparison or GPU work.\n\n### Validation\n\nParent `99f802f300c80fed8e10bd8dd670d478b1bec598`; candidate `7ce445369384a59a8d833c964dac1a59cfd83b84`.\n\n- Four maintained test groups pass using refreshed production source and `-Werror` build flags.\n- Generated mapping GLSL compiles at workgroups1/256 and passes SPIR-V validation.\n- Independent source review and diff whitespace check pass.\n- Exact-head CI running. Historical checks do not replace it.\n\n### Results\n\nThe checked cases accept the intended pair and reject incompatible inputs. Performance: N/A for this unused pure helper layer. Native image conversion, queue ownership and guest-visible behavior are qualified in the consuming layers rather than inferred from these tests.\n\n### Risks and remaining questions\n\nAdmission alone cannot detect a newer overlapping producer or establish RAM ownership. #289 additionally rejects views too small for its four-pixel stencil unpack; #290 must establish runtime ownership. None of these checks establishes a game FPS gain.\n\n[Current evidence](https://github.com/Mainkill1/xemu/tree/b54b877162/evidence/alias-merge-train-20261006/pr288) is outside main.\n\n### Related work\n\nHOLD on #287. Prerequisite for #289/#290. Addresses #285 without closing the performance investigation.\n\n> **Agent Declaration**: This pull request was created with assistance from OpenAI Codex (GPT-6).\n",
